  "_notes": [
    "Two feed kinds are supported:",
    "  'rss'        -> a direct RSS/Atom URL.",
    "  'googlenews' -> a topical query turned into a Google News RSS feed.",
    "Google News is used as a robust catch-all for sources that have no free RSS",
    "or are paywalled (FT, Times, Telegraph premium, CoStar, Green Street, Estates",
    "Gazette, Property Week, Bisnow, JSE SENS). It reliably returns recent items",
    "server-side. Edit freely: add/remove feeds, change queries, retune weights.",
    "Each feed has: id, kind, name (display source), url|query, section, geo, weight."
